  "description": "v031's exact recipe with ONE change: hidden 128 -> 96, so 225,922 -> 148,674 params, a 34% reduction. Every other scalar identical: distill_weight 2.0, input_proj 64, 3 epochs, same teacher, schedule, LR and seed.",
  "hypothesis": "THE ONLY CAPACITY DIRECTION THAT HAS EVER WORKED, and it has never been tested past its current endpoint. Every capacity experiment in this project has gone UP and every one has lost: head 192->384 -3.2 sigma, hidden 128->285 -13.7, hidden 128->415 -21.7. We have never gone DOWN.\n\n  Going down has exactly one precedent and it points this way. v022 (321,602 params) and v023 (225,922) shared distill_weight 0.5 -- locally v022 was 0.000547 BETTER, and publicly v023 was 0.0003 better while running 10% faster. So on the board that matters, smaller was ahead, on a single submission each, which is weak evidence, but it is the only direction with a positive sign and it also buys latency.\n\n  Prediction: 96 units scores within noise of v031 locally, and if the public trend is real it beats it while cutting per-row compute roughly 20%. A loss here would NOT be surprising and would mean 128 is a genuine interior optimum, which is itself worth knowing -- it would say the model is neither too big nor too small and the remaining gap to the leader is not a capacity problem at all.",
  "change_vs_parent": "model.hidden 128 -> 96 only. Param count falls 225,922 -> 148,674, a 34% reduction, leaving 34.1% of the 435,943-param teacher.",
